{
  "_comment": [
    "Cimmeria MCP server configuration template.",
    "",
    "Copy this file to .mcp.json (which is gitignored) and replace the",
    "<CIMMERIA_ROOT> placeholders with the absolute path to your repo checkout.",
    "On Windows that looks like: C:\\Users\\you\\source\\projects\\Cimmeria",
    "",
    "If you ran `pwsh setup.ps1 -WithReToolchain`, this file was generated for",
    "you automatically — no manual edits required. See:",
    "  docs/guides/re-toolchain-setup.md     -- end-to-end setup",
    "  docs/guides/reverse-engineering-with-claude.md  -- the workflow doc",
    "",
    "Five servers are wired:",
    "  cimmeria-rag : Azure-hosted RAG over the Cimmeria repo + docs + RE notes.",
    "                 Read-only. No local dependencies. Always reachable.",
    "  ghidra       : Static analysis of SGW.exe via the bethington/ghidra-mcp",
    "                 bridge. Requires Ghidra GUI running with the GhidraMCP",
    "                 plugin server started.",
    "  x64dbg       : Dynamic analysis via dariushoule/x64dbg-automate. Requires",
    "                 x96dbg.exe launched with the x64dbg-automate plugin loaded.",
    "  cimmeria-lab : Live Research Lab supervisor (stdio). Drives a running",
    "                 SGW.exe on this dev box: Lua eval, non-freezing hooks,",
    "                 screenshots, autologin, and the merged timeline. Windows",
    "                 only. Build once: cargo build -p cimmeria-lab. See",
    "                 docs/guides/live-research-lab.md and re-toolchain-setup.md.",
    "  lab-server   : In-server lab endpoint (http, token-gated). Live entity /",
    "                 witness / packet-tap / dot-console reads from a running",
    "                 cimmeria-server. Only present when the server was started",
    "                 with CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_BIND + CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN set",
    "                 (fail-closed). On the colo it is reachable over WireGuard",
    "                 only -- see docs/operations/colo-deploy.md.",
    "",
    "The GHIDRA_MCP_URL port can drift on Windows when iphlpsvc holds 8089-8099.",
    "The plugin falls back to the first free port in 8089..8104 — confirm the",
    "actual bound port from Ghidra's console output, not the status dialog",
    "(upstream display bug shows the configured port, not the bound one)."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "cimmeria-rag": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://cimmeria-mcp.azurewebsites.net/runtime/webhooks/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "x-functions-key": "REPLACE_WITH_FUNCTIONS_KEY"
      }
    },
    "ghidra": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\.venvs\\ghidra-mcp\\Scripts\\python.exe",
      "args": [
        "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\external\\ghidra-mcp\\bridge_mcp_ghidra.py"
      ],
      "env": {
        "GHIDRA_MCP_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8100/"
      }
    },
    "x64dbg": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\.venvs\\x64dbg-mcp\\Scripts\\x64dbg-automate-mcp.exe",
      "env": {
        "X64DBG_PATH": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\dbg\\release\\x96dbg.exe"
      }
    },
    "cimmeria-lab": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\target\\debug\\cimmeria-lab.exe",
      "env": {
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_INSTALL_DIR": "<SGW_INSTALL_DIR>",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_BRIDGE": "127.0.0.1:8770",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8444/mcp",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN": "REPLACE_WITH_LAB_MCP_TOKEN_32B_MIN"
      }
    },
    "lab-server": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8444/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer REPLACE_WITH_LAB_MCP_TOKEN_32B_MIN"
      }
    }
  }
}
